    # Antigravity Rules

    Global operational constraints and token economy standards for AI coding agents:

    - Zero-Emoji: Never use emojis in code, comments, commit messages, or documentation.
    - Zero AI Slop: Eliminate conversational filler, pleasantries, and meta-announcements.
    - Targeted Reading: Inspect specific files and line ranges only; no blind directory scans.
    - Plan Threshold: For tasks touching > 2 files, output a 5-line plan and wait for confirmation.
    - Terminal Output Cap: Cap CLI logs to 40 lines and append quiet flags (`--quiet`, `-q`).
    - Two-Strike Debugging: Stop after 2 consecutive failed attempts and analyze root causes.
    - Anti-Placeholder: Zero incomplete stubs or `// TODO` stubs in production paths.

    Full configuration kit, on-demand skills, and installers:
    https://github.com/davidyehuda45-byte/antigravity-rules
